{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\":\"    def estimate_join_cost(\\n        self,\\n        left_rows: int,\\n        right_rows: int,\\n        selectivity: float,\\n    ) -> float:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Estimate the output cardinality for a join operation.\\n\\n        The formula is:  left_rows * right_rows * selectivity\\n\\n        BUG_50: selectivity is applied twice, inflating the cost estimate\\n        and causing the optimizer to reject valid hash-join plans.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        cost = left_rows * right_rows * selectivity\\n        self.emit_metric(\\\"query.plan.estimated_cost\\\", cost)\\n        self._history.append(\\n            JoinStats(\\n                left_rows=left_rows,\\n                right_rows=right_rows,\\n                selectivity=selectivity,\\n                estimated_cost=cost,\\n            )\\n        )\\n        return cost\\n\",\"comments\":\"Apply selectivity only once and emit the planned cost metric before recording the history entry.\"}"}}
